hello pilots let's discuss superiority  and battles advantage points the  important role of attack aircraft and  how concealment works let's start with  the basics  your team can achieve victory and a  standard battle either by destroying all  enemy aircraft or gaining supremacy so  what is superiority and how can you gain  it first of all you need to score  advantage points you do this by  destroying enemy targets both on the  ground and in the air one destroyed  aircraft will bring one point to your  team the same for destroying a ground  target and three points for a  headquarters at the top of the screen  you can see the so called supremacy  meter that displays each team's current  battle progress at the beginning of the  battle this bar is empty it begins to  fill after each team starts scoring  points a team that achieves 100%  superiority wins the battle if the enemy  team has more advantage points but loses  all their aircraft your team wins  regardless of the number of advantage  points the battle can come to a draw  when either the bar remains equal after  the end of the 15-minute battle or all  aircraft on both teams are destroyed if  the enemy team destroys a friendly  aircraft or ground target your team will  lose some part of the supremacy meter  filling a team loses 15% advantage if  one of their aircraft is destroyed a  destroyed ground target cost 30%  advantage a team loses 90 percent  advantage if their headquarters is  destroyed how fast the bar fills depends  on the difference in advantage points of  both teams let's look at an example  team a lost for aircraft while Team B  lost one aircraft it means that the  score is one to four team B is leading  by three points the supremacy meter of  Team B fills at 0.8% per second so team  a has about a minute and a half to score  points suppose Team a destroys a small  ground target the score is now two to  four with team be having a two-point  advantage the supremacy meter of Team B  drops by 30% and starts filling again at  0.6% per second then Team B destroys  team a's headquarters the score is now 2  to 7 and Team B has a 5 point advantage  their supremacy meter continues filling  but faster at one point 2 percent per  second  attack aircraft are very important for  cheating and maintaining advantage this  is the most controversial aircraft type  in the game attack aircraft carry  powerful weapons and have high  durability many also have a rear gunner  however their low speed and  maneuverability as well as low optimum  altitude compensate for it low optimum  altitude is both a strong and a weak  point though it's all about aircraft  concealment an aircraft flying low to  the ground is harder to detect different  aircraft types have different  concealment effectiveness attack  aircraft have the best concealment if an  aircraft flies at an altitude of 200  meters or lower they receive concealment  bonus the lower they fly the higher the  bonus is dropping bombs does not affect  concealment aircraft lose concealment  when they open fire or launch rockets  concealment begins to work again and a  few seconds after aircraft have stopped  fire if an aircraft is set on fire  flames and smoke will give it away  attack aircraft are the most effective  aircrafts type in destroying ground  targets even when using machine gun and  autocannon by the way have you noticed  that the same buildings or a a guns on  the same map may have different levels  of hit points let's find out why every  ground target type has standard  durability that increases depending on  the tier of the battle it is calculated  by a simple formula multiplied your  ability by X where X is the highest  aircraft tier in the battle let's take  an AAA gun for example if the highest  aircraft tier in the battle is tier 1  the AAA gun will have 150 hit points if  the highest aircraft's tier and the  battle is tier 10 the AAA gun will have  1500 hit points now let's move from  theory to practice here are several  examples of how to conduct battle when  the enemy team has advantage for  instance let's look at if only enemy  aircraft are left and you're flying a  fighter look for enemy aircraft while  flying at about 500 meters above the  ground most likely they'll be flying  along map borders check the area around  the enemy base but try to avoid enemy  AAA guns occasionally enemy attack  aircraft won't be too cunning you will  likely find them near your ground  targets when you get advantage enemy  aircraft will try to knock it down as  soon as an enemy attack  a friendly ground target it will be  displayed on the mini-map enemy aircraft  will be revealed so you will be able to  catch up with it and bring it down the  opposite situation you're flying an  attack aircraft while there are only  enemy fighters left you should carefully  move to the nearest enemy a a gun or  other ground target if enemy aircraft  haven't been spotted in that area if  your team has only a narrow advantage  destroy a few ground targets and quickly  fly to another area usually the speed of  your actions matters the most in this  situation destroy already damaged ground  targets ideally the damaged enemy  headquarters do 1 attack run and move to  a different area  you shouldn't simply cruise around if  both you and your enemies are flying  attack aircraft the best you can do is  to destroy ground targets while  monitoring the activity of Allied aaaa  guns on your mini-map if the enemy  suddenly stops destroying friendly  ground targets and you already have  advantage you should fly away there is  no guarantee that you bring enemy  aircrafts down what matters here is  patience if enemy aircraft keep  destroying your ground targets there's a  chance they will crash or will be  destroyed by friendly AAA guns just  don't crash yourself if the enemy team  has a fighter or a heavy fighter left it  could take too much time to find them  they may be flying at high altitude you  should destroy ground targets even if  you fly a fighter start with the ground  targets that have the least amount of  hit points  remember to monitor your mini-map and  radar enemy fighters may come back to  destroy aircraft that attack ground  targets here's another example the enemy  team has an 80% advantage none of your  allies are destroying ground targets you  spot an undamaged enemy aircraft and  realize that you don't have enough  firepower to destroy it quickly in this  case ramming is a viable option you'll  not only be able to knock down the enemy  advantage but pull a victory for your  team we hope that this information will  help you choose the right tactical  solutions stay less detectable survive  more often and get more enjoyment from  the game that's all for now good luck in  your battles  you
 

